<Alert Color="Color.Warning" Visible>
    <AlertDescription>
        <Strong>Never use a License Key as the value of <Code>ProductToken</Code> or place a License Key in application code, configuration, deployment files, or client-side assets.</Strong>
    </AlertDescription>
</Alert>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    See <Anchor To="docs/usage/licensing/register-product-token#protecting-your-producttoken" Title="Protecting your ProductToken">Protecting your ProductToken</Anchor> for storage, local development, production, CI/CD, and Blazor WebAssembly guidance.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    License behavior
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    A valid commercial ProductToken removes licensing warnings and licensed component limits. An existing Community ProductToken applies the original Community license and displays a compact <Strong>Community License</Strong> button in the bottom-right corner. Select the button to open the full license notice.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    A missing or invalid ProductToken is treated as unlicensed and displays the applicable warning and component limits. An expired token displays the applicable expired-license notice.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Get a ProductToken
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Follow the <Anchor To="docs/usage/licensing/register-product-token" Title="Configure a ProductToken">ProductToken configuration guide</Anchor> to get a ProductToken from your Blazorise account and configure your application.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Indie project licensing
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    <Strong>Indie</Strong> is an annual license for one registered product or application. It covers one developer working on an independently owned project with annual project revenue below €25,000. Personal and commercial projects can qualify; client and agency work are excluded.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    A valid Indie ProductToken removes evaluation component limits and the licensing banner for the registered project. Indie does not include dedicated support, private repositories, Themes, Blocks, or other premium benefits.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    If annual project revenue exceeds €25,000, upgrade to Professional at the next renewal. See <Anchor To="indie">Indie eligibility</Anchor> for details.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Your Indie ProductToken contains the registered project name and its permitted application assemblies. Set <Code>BlazoriseOptions.ProductAssembly</Code> to an assembly from your application so Blazorise can match it to the token. See the Indie section of the <Anchor To="docs/usage/licensing/register-product-token">ProductToken configuration guide</Anchor> for setup, assembly naming, and applications with multiple hosts.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Component limits
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Evaluation limits apply without a valid ProductToken. The paid plans below remove these limits within their licensed scope. Existing Community tokens retain their original terms and limits.
</DocsPageParagraph>

